+/// Like analyze(), but lays the padded code + JUMPDEST bitset into the
+/// caller-provided @p buffer (capacity @p capacity bytes) instead of allocating
+/// on the heap. Used by the ZisK analysis cache so per-contract analyses live in
+/// a fixed, reusable arena rather than growing the heap. The returned
+/// CodeAnalysis's padded-code unique_ptr adopts @p buffer; the caller owns the
+/// buffer and MUST NOT let the CodeAnalysis be destroyed (the cache reuses slots
+/// by placement-new, never destruction). Fatals if @p capacity is too small.
+EVMC_EXPORT CodeAnalysis analyze_into(bytes_view code, uint8_t* buffer, size_t capacity);
